From 88a6b405c797711f07dd8ea6d307e65d61bc85cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retrorepair <joelwhybrow@googlemail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:52:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] input: the light-gun beacon - hold the trigger, ask the core
 for a white flash, measure, then give the core the aim and the trigger
 together

A CRT gun reads only where there is light. A dark enemy or dark patch gave it nothing, so the aim fell back to the last bright spot (dark
enemies were not hit) and an off-screen shot could not be told from a dark one (the reload lottery). Virtua Cop's own flash is a black frame,
and the arcade cabinet's gun board put a flash into the video path itself. For cores that can show the picture white on request (joystick_3
bit 0; the Model 2 core) the tracker now holds the trigger back on a pull, asks for the flash, collects the readings (a steady gun reports
nothing new, so its last report counts; the junk first report after darkness is rejected), and after about 55 ms gives the core the aim, or
OFF-SCREEN if the whole picture was white and the gun saw none of it, and then the trigger. LIGHTGUN_CRT_BEACON=0 turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
